      "id": "PM-09",
      "title": "DCMA-14 Schedule Quality Audit & Longest Path Diagnostics",
      "desc": "Enforce 100% logic integrity: zero dangling open ends, zero arbitrary lags/constraints, positive float discipline, and realistic critical density.",
      "tags": [
        "DCMA-14",
        "Schedule QA"
      ],
      "folder": "Phase_2_Planning_WBS_P6_RIBA_2_3\\PM-09_DCMA14_Schedule_Quality_Audit",
      "keyFacts": [
        "DCMA-14 Score: 6/6 Automated Health Audit Checks PASS",
        "Logic Targets: 0% Open Ends | 0% Leads | 0% Negative Float",
        "High Float (>44d): <= 44% threshold monitored monthly",
        "Constraints: Hard constraints <= 5% (milestones justified only)",
        "Schedule QRA: Monte Carlo P50 / P80 float-path buffer validation"
      ],
      "readme": "# PM-09: DCMA-14 Schedule Quality Audit & Longest Path Diagnostics\n\n- **Phase**: `Phase 2: Planning, WBS & Master Schedule (RIBA 2-3)`\n- **RIBA Stage**: `RIBA Stage 2-5`\n- **P6 Milestone Gate**: `880 Workdays`\n- **WBS Scope**: `All WBS`\n- **Governing Standards**: DCMA 14-Point Schedule Assessment Standard (6/6 Automated Pass)\n- **Focus Areas**: Logic Density, Zero Open Ends, Zero Constraints, High Float <= 44%, Longest Path\n\n## Module Overview\nEnforce 100% logic integrity: zero dangling open ends, zero arbitrary lags/constraints, positive float discipline, and realistic critical density.\n\n## Ordered Flashcard Documents (`Doc 1` -> `Doc 4`)\n\n| Doc | Category | Title | Exact Local File | Companion / Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Doc 1 | Standard | DCMA 14-Point Schedule Assessment Guideline (Logic, Leads, Lags, Float) | `PM09_Doc1_Standard_DCMA_14_Point_Schedule_Assessment_Rev.004.docx` | DCMA 14-Point Standard |\n| Doc 2 | Deliverable | Automated DCMA-14 6/6 Schedule Health Diagnostic Report (pyp6xer Log) | `PM09_Doc2_Deliverable_DCMA14_Schedule_Baseline_XER_Master_Rev.004.xer` | pyp6xer Quality Engine |\n| Doc 3 | Template | Monthly Contractor Schedule Update Audit & Float Consumption Checksheet | `PM09_Doc3_Template_Monthly_Contractor_Schedule_Update_Rev.004.xlsx` | Clause 31/32 Schedule Check |\n| Doc 4 | Audit | Driving Predecessor & Near-Critical Path Risk Diagnostic Sheet | `PM09_Doc4_Audit_Driving_Predecessor_Near_Critical_Rev.004.xlsx` | Longest Path Trace |\n\n## Study Takeaway (`Why Each Document Matters`)\n- **Doc 1 (Standard)**: Learn exact thresholds (<5% high float, 0% negative float, 0 lags) for lender audits.\n- **Doc 2 (Deliverable)**: Inspect verified proof of zero open ends, zero hard constraints, and valid critical density.\n- **Doc 3 (Template)**: Spot hidden logic overrides, artificial lags, and silent float erosion each reporting cycle.\n- **Doc 4 (Audit)**: Isolate tasks with <10 days total float likely to flip onto the driving critical path.\n",
